{
  "title": "Fix Open Food Facts aisle quirks",
  "description": "A line that neither the catalog nor a learned answer places gets its aisle from Open Food Facts (data/open_food_facts.json), and a spot check found these wrong: butter variants ('sweet butter' -> Produce, 'garlic butter' and 'European-style butter' -> Oils & Vinegars), 'diced tomatoes with green chiles' -> Produce, pecans ('pecan chips', 'shelled pecans') -> Snacks, 'lemon pepper' -> Meat & Seafood, 'ginger juice' -> Beverages, 'fish stock' -> Spices & Seasonings, 'Seasonings' -> Condiments & Sauces, 'juniper berries' -> Condiments & Sauces. \
Most come from product-name or brand votes rather than the taxonomy; look for a systematic fix in scripts/import-open-food-facts.py or open_food_facts_aisles.json before adding catalog entries one by one. \
The shopping-list scorecard (make shopping-list-categorizer-test) reports wrong aisles apart from missing ones; its two wrong aisles are 'Dip' -> Cheese (Open Food Facts) and 'Ground flaxseed' -> Nuts & Dried Fruit (debatable label).",
